@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+## Context
+
+`OrderService.place` records a single-use coupon under the new order id (`coupons.use(code, id)`), but
+`cancel` calls `coupons.giveBack(code, order.customer)`. `Coupons.giveBack` only releases when the recorded
+order matches, so it never releases. Shipping (`shippingCost`, `priceOrder`) already compares goods after
+discounts with 5000 cents using `>=`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Fix at the call site: pass `id` instead of `order.customer` in `cancel`. `Coupons.giveBack` stays unchanged.
+- No code change for shipping; the reported case is consistent with the README (threshold on goods after
+  discounts). Pin it with tests rather than alter the rule. If support's case turns out to be something else
+  (goods really >= €50.00 after discounts), it needs a reproduction, outside this change.
+- Money stays in integer cents; no new dependencies.
+
+## Risks
+
+Minimal: one argument changed. Orders without a coupon are unaffected.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-09-fix-coupon-giveback-and-free-shipping/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-09-fix-coupon-giveback-and-free-shipping/proposal.md
