+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-09-fix-coupon-giveback-and-free-shipping/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+## Why
+
+Two customer reports. (1) A customer cancelled an order that used a single-use welcome coupon and the
+coupon was then refused as "already used" on the corrected order. The cause: `OrderService.cancel` gives
+the coupon back under the customer's name, but the coupon was recorded under the order id, so the give-back
+never matches. (2) A customer paid €4.90 shipping on an order "of exactly €50". The code already ships free
+at goods >= 5000 cents after discounts (and a test covers it); the likely cause is an order whose lines came
+to €50.00 *before* a discount, so goods after discounts were below €50.00 — which the README says is paid
+shipping.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Fix cancellation so a single-use coupon is given back to the order that used it (code fix in `src/orders.ts`).
+- Report 2: no behaviour change. Add regression tests pinning the boundary on goods *after* discounts
+  (gross €50.00 with a discount pays shipping; goods of exactly €50.00 after a discount ship free).
+- No README change: the README already states both rules correctly.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- `coupons`: add the requirement that cancelling an order makes its single-use coupon usable again.
+- `shipping`: add a scenario clarifying that the €50.00 threshold applies to goods after discounts.
+
+## Impact
+
+README business rules affected: Orders (cancellation gives back the coupon), Discounts (single-use coupon),
+Shipping (free from €50.00 after discounts) — all are restated, none altered. Code: `src/orders.ts`;
+tests: `test/orders.test.ts`.
+
+Out of scope: any other rule, VAT on shipping, changing the free-shipping threshold, coupon rules other
+than give-back, and the cancellation window.
